meta {
  name: Create Product - Full Featured
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "sku": "WC-TEST-FULL-001",
    "label": "WC Test Full Product",
    "category_ids": ["6a9f1b482b6fd055ffb7c7dc", "6a9f1b542b6fd055ffb7c7dd"],
    "attributes": {"wc_test_text": "WC full-featured test value"},
    "thumbnail_id": "6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.thumbnail_id: eq 6aa021b72b6fd055ffb7ca9f
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against "David's Dev Account", wiring together
  every kept fixture from Phase 1 and Phase 2a. **Fixture kept** -- id
  `6aa022262b6fd055ffb7caa4`, for Phase 3/4 (Pim Product Lists, Channels,
  Ecatalogs, etc.) to have something real to query.
  
  `201 Created`.
  
  ## attributes map is keyed by attribute NAME, not id
  `{"attributes": {"wc_test_text": "..."}}` -- confirmed via a separate
  scratch product (created and deleted in this same test run) that this
  is the expected key, not the attribute's Mongo `id`. The response's
  `attributes` map also includes several pre-existing system/completeness
  attributes not sent in this request (`amazon_ready`,
  `basic_information_completeness`, `website_ready`, etc., all numeric
  scores) -- these appear to be account-level default attributes applied
  to every product automatically, not something this request created.
  
  ## category_ids DOES link on create -- differs from assets
  Unlike `09-Assets/Create Asset.bru` (where the identical `category_ids`
  field is silently ignored on `POST`), it **works immediately** here: a
  follow-up `GET /products/{id}/categories` shows both categories fully
  linked. Confirms the create-time relationship-linking behavior is
  resource-specific, not a blanket rule either way.
  
  ## thumbnail_id also persists on create
  Unlike the array-typed `category_ids` on assets, this single-reference
  field round-trips correctly in the create response itself.
  
  ## Not idempotent to re-run
  `sku` is unique per account. Re-running this request once the fixture
  exists returns `409 Conflict {"errors":[{"name":"AlreadyExists",
  "description":"product data validation failed"}]}` -- same
  `409`/`AlreadyExists` family as attribute groups/attributes (Phase 1),
  not categories' `422` (`config/api-testing.config.md` quirk #33).
}
